From: evilcomputer12 <martinrobotika@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 02:02:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/19] xgameruntime: Real Xbox Live identity and
 XUserGetTokenAndSignature in XUser.

Identity: the first XUserAddAsync asks xodus-service who is signed in
(UserInfoRequest with the title's MSAAppId and decimal TitleId, 15 s cap)
from the worker thread that completes the XAsyncBlock. With SignedIn=true
the single local user becomes that account: XUserGetId returns the XUID,
XUserGetGamertag the classic/modern/suffix/unique components, and
XUserGetAgeGroup the reported age group. Without a service, with
XODUS_OFFLINE=1, when nobody is signed in, or on any error or timeout the
offline user stays exactly as before (XUID 0x0009000000000001, OS user
name, Adult); later XUserAddAsync calls retry until a sign-in was seen.
XUserGetGamertag now honours the component argument, is UTF-8 aware and
reports the needed size on E_NOT_SUFFICIENT_BUFFER.

Tokens: XUserGetTokenAndSignatureAsync/ResultSize/Result and the Utf16
variants forward the game's request (method, url, headers, raw body,
ForceRefresh) to the service through TokenAndSignatureRequest on a worker
thread (XGameSave's async pattern), with a 60 s cap. The result is packed
into the caller's buffer: XUserGetTokenAndSignatureData, then the
NUL-terminated token and signature, pointers into the same buffer; an
empty signature is NULL/0. A service <Error> completes the block with that
HRESULT (E_GAMEUSER_SIGNED_OUT, E_GAMEUSER_RESOLVE_USER_ISSUE_REQUIRED, ...),
transport failures with E_GAMEUSER_FAILED_TO_GET_TOKEN. While no real user
is known the calls keep returning E_NOTIMPL as before. Token and signature
values are never traced.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
